-- title:
--   Igusa-side end of a node: branch prolongation and its centre
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. the image of $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$. Write $\kappa$ for the residue field of $A$, $A_0$ for the valuation subring $A \cap k_0$ obtained by pulling $A$ back along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ (for the intermediate field $k_0$ introduced below), $\mathcal C := \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ for the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\kappa$ generated over $\kappa$ by the two series `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'` $= \mathrm{qExpand}\,\kappa\,M'(\mathtt{jqModC}\,\kappa)$, $\overline F_{M'} := \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ for the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field $\mathbb Q\bigl(\mathrm{qExpand}_d\,j_q : d \mid M'\bigr)$, and $\mathcal F := \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M' = \mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$ for the corresponding base change of the function field of the level-$q^2M'$ curve attached to the subgroup $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M' \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$, the kernel of the unit-group reduction along `dvd_sq_mul q M'`. A `Place K F` is a proper valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$ whose ring is a principal ideal ring; `ord`, `evalAt` and `IsRational` are its order function, its $K$-valued evaluation map and the condition that $K$ surject onto its residue field.
--
--   The data fixed before the conclusion are: a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathcal C$ over $\kappa$ with `hW` asserting that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places, i.e. of those $w$ which are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M'` and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathtt{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M') \in \mathtt{ssJSet}\,q\,\kappa$; the inclusion `hle` of $\overline F_{M'}$ in $\mathcal F$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ on $\overline F_{M'}$ with values in $\mathcal C$, that is, a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\overline F_{M'}$ together with a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto $\mathcal C$ with kernel the maximal ideal, a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors of functions with nonzero residue, tracing $A$ on constants and inducing there the residue map of $A$, and admitting for each nonzero $f$ a constant $c$ with $c\cdot f$ integral of nonzero residue; the hypothesis `hR₀`, saying that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\overline F_{M'}$ is $R_0$-integral with $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; a chosen element $s$ of $W$; and the hypothesis `hGU`, which characterises $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ as the Gauss ring in the $q$-expansion $j_q$: any valuation subring $V$ of $\overline F_{M'}$ which traces $A$ on constants, contains the image of $j_q$, and has the property that for every polynomial over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with all coefficients in $A$ whose value at that image lies in $\mathfrak m_V$ all coefficients already lie in $\mathfrak m_V$, has the same elements as $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$.
--
--   The constants group consists of an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$ (`hπ`), together with the hypotheses that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and `hκ`, that every $a \in A$ differs from some element of $k_0 \cap A$ by an element of $\mathfrak m_A$.
--
--   With $\mathcal F$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is universally quantified over the following further data. First, an intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathcal F/k_0$ subject to two conditions: generation, $\mathrm{adjoin}_{k_0}(\mathrm{range}(\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathcal F)) \sqcup F_0 = \top$; and linear disjointness, namely for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathcal F$ with all $a_i$ in $\mathrm{adjoin}_{k_0}(\text{image of }K') \sqcup F_0$, if $c$ is $K'$-linearly independent and $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ then all $a_i = 0$.
--
--   Second, a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ for which the conjunction holds: $W_0$ traces $A$ on $k_0$ (for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ iff its image lies in $W_0$), $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, and the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$.
--
--   Third, a local noetherian subring $O$ of $F_0$ with: $O \subseteq W_0$; $O$ traces $A$ on $k_0$; for every $f \in O$ there is $x \in k_0 \cap A$ with image in $O$ such that $f - x$ is a nonunit of $O$; and every $f \in F_0$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in O$, $h \ne 0$.
--
--   Fourth, the crossing presentation: an integer $E_0 \ge 1$, a proof `hπO` that the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $O$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}(\widehat{A_0}, \pi_0^{E_0}) = \widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi_0^{E_0})$ (with $\widehat{A_0}$ the adic completion of $A_0$), and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that quotient, subject to: $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$; $\iota$ sends each constant $x \in k_0 \cap A$ lying in $O$ to $\mathrm{const}(x)$; $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V$; and $c_y \in W_0$ with $c_y \in \mathfrak m_{W_0}$, while $c_x$, whenever it lies in $W_0$, is not in $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$.
--
--   Fifth, the Igusa branch: a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ with $O \subseteq W_x$, tracing $A$ on $k_0$, a discrete valuation ring, whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$, residually transcendental in the sense that there is $t \in W_x$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t) \in \mathfrak m_{W_x}$ then every coefficient of $p$ lies in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$; with $c_x \in \mathfrak m_{W_x}$ and $c_y \notin \mathfrak m_{W_x}$; and satisfying the level-$M'$ reading laws: for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ lying in the full level-$M'$ modular function field, whose image in $\overline F_{M'}$ is $R_0$-integral (witness `hgi`) and is regular at every place of $\overline F_{M'}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j_q$ is regular, the image of $g$ in $\mathcal F$ lies in $F_0$, that element lies in $W_x$, it lies in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ if and only if $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(g) = 0$, and if $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(g)$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ then the element lies in $O$ and, for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ with image in $O$ whose $A$-residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(g))$, the difference of the two elements of $O$ is a nonunit.
--
--   Finally, a field $F_{SS}$ which is a $\kappa$-algebra and a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ on $\mathcal F$ with values in $F_{SS}$ — a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\mathcal F$ with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $F_{SS}$ with kernel the maximal ideal, tracing $A$ on constants, inducing the residue map of $A$ there, and with the scaling property for nonzero elements — such that for $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $f \in W_0$.
--
--   Under all of this there exist a field $FI$, a $\kappa$-algebra structure on it, a regular prolongation $R_x$ of $A$ on $\mathcal F$ with values in $FI$, and a place $b_x$ of $FI$ over $\kappa$ such that:
--
--   (i) for $f \in F_0$, $f \in R_x.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $f \in W_x$;
--
--   (ii) $b_x$ is rational, i.e. $\kappa$ surjects onto the residue field of $b_x$;
--
--   (iii) for every $f \in F_0$ lying in $O$ and $R_x$-integral, $R_x.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ lies in the valuation subring of $b_x$;
--
--   (iv) for every $f \in F_0$ lying in $O$ and $R_x$-integral which is a nonunit of $O$, $R_x.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ lies in the valuation subring of $b_x$ and in its maximal ideal;
--
--   (v) $b_x$ is the only place of $FI$ over $\kappa$ with properties (iii) and (iv): any place $y$ satisfying the two displayed conditions with $y$ in place of $b_x$ equals $b_x$;
--
--   (vi) whenever the image of $c_x$ in $\mathcal F$ is $R_x$-integral, its $R_x$-residue is $0$;
--
--   (vii) whenever the image of $c_y$ in $\mathcal F$ is $R_x$-integral, $b_x.\mathrm{ord}$ of its $R_x$-residue equals $1$;
--
--   (viii) every $R_0$-integral element of $\overline F_{M'}$ has $R_x$-integral image in $\mathcal F$ under the inclusion given by `hle`;
--
--   (ix) there is a ring homomorphism $j : \mathcal C \to FI$ such that for every $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ the image of $f$ in $\mathcal F$ is $R_x$-integral with $R_x.\mathrm{residue}$ equal to $j(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f))$, and such that for every $g \in \mathcal C$ one has $g$ in the valuation subring of $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ lies in the valuation subring of $b_x$.
--
--   This is the Igusa-branch half of the local analysis at one node of the semistable model of the level-$q^2M'$ modular curve over the valuation ring $A$: from a crossing presentation $\widehat O \cong \widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$ of the node together with the branch valuation ring $W_x$ on which the Igusa coordinate $c_x$ vanishes, it produces a regular prolongation $R_x$ realising $W_x$ on $F_0$, the unique place $b_x$ of its residue field centred at the node, the vanishing and order-one laws for the two node coordinates, and a compatible embedding of the level-$M'$ reduction field $\mathcal C$ matching the supersingular place $s$ with $b_x$. It is used in the assembly of the node charts for that model, via the two declarations that cite it.
